    "title": "Longstreet Texas, the \"King of the Texas Blues\" and The Huntsville Connection",
    "text": "Longstreet, Texas, is now just a precinct house off Highway 149, some 20 miles southwest of Huntsville.\nHowever, the name rides the crest of a bountiful history. In its prime, its streets saw gun battles, while its saloons waxed rowdy. For example, two sisters married brothers, both of whom met death by a shootout on Main Street. On moving to another town, the sisters remarried only to see each of their husbands again die in a gunfight.",
